# Page TSconfig of this extension, auto-included for the whole installation.
#
# TYPO3 reads "Configuration/page.tsconfig" of every active extension since
# v12.0 (Feature: #96614), so it is read on both core versions this extension
# supports. This file is the place for everything an installation needs
# regardless of its site configuration.
#
# The content element group header is exactly that: every academic extension
# sorts its content elements into the group "academic", so the group has to
# carry its label on every installation, not only on the sites that enable the
# set "fgtclb/academic-base-ctype-group" (ACE-453) - and site sets arrived in
# TYPO3 v13.1, so on v12 they deliver nothing at all. The very same file is
# also reachable through that set and through the page field "Page TSconfig" -
# one physical copy, three ways to it, and assigning the same two values again
# changes nothing.
@import 'EXT:academic_base/Configuration/TSconfig/CTypeGroup/page.tsconfig'
